(5899158, 852224, 15407, '<td valign="top">I tooka similar picture quite awhile back and wonder what you created your "mount" with?<br/>Tim <br/>The battery in the bike died so I had to push start it... thus the One in the morning indication was really one in the afternoon!<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpch" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.dpch</a><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=69671" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=69671</a></td>', 'I tooka similar picture quite awhile back and wonder what you created your "mount" with?Tim The battery in the bike died so I had to push start it... thus the One in the morning indication was really one in the afternoon! //www.dpch//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=69671', '2010-03-10 19:45:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5899349, 852224, 23579, '<td valign="top">I made it out of plastic. The base screws on top of the gas tank cap (where the existing screws are). A ball head is screwed on top of the mount to support the camera. Check out a picture <a href="//picasaweb.google.com/lh/photo/7mGuncIE9cm2PBSvPF0udw?feat=directlink" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">here</a>.<br/> <br/>The camera sits pretty high off the tank. It had to be that high to see over the handle bars. I sometimes hit the top of the camera with my chin while riding.</td>', 'I made it out of plastic. The base screws on top of the gas tank cap (where the existing screws are). A ball head is screwed on top of the mount to support the camera. Check out a picture here. The camera sits pretty high off the tank. It had to be that high to see over the handle bars. I sometimes hit the top of the camera with my chin while riding.', '2010-03-10 22:10:01.000000', NULL, 0),
